      },
      {
        "id": 5835,
        "name": "Fight Night 2004",
        "summary": "Fight Night is EA Sports' new boxing series, replacing the previous Knockout Kings line of games.\n\nYou have the option of creating your own personalized boxer, and entering a career mode, where you start off on the lowest rung in dirty, rundown gyms, as you make your way up the ropes to become the undisputed champion. Throughout your career you will have to battle many enemies, all vying for the same title. As you play, you will be able to train, improving your boxer's stats. You can hit a punching bag to increase power and speed, spar with an opponent for more stamina and agility, attack the dummy to improve chin and body, or hit the mitts to improve heart and cut. Besides career mode, you have access to the standard modes.\n\nFight Night 2004 features the \"Total Control\" system, which utilizes both sticks to give you complete percision over your boxer's moves. The right analog stick controls all the punching, and the left stick controls movement and defense/blocks.\n\nThere are several unlockables available, all of which must be earned through career mode. You can buy new clothes, entrance music, even new girls to accompany you to the ring.\n\nThe PlayStation 2 version of Fight Night 2004 supports online play via EA Sports' online network.\n\nAs with all other EA Sports titles, Fight Night 2004 utilizes the EA Sports Bio, which tracks your progress through all EA Sports games. The more games you play, the longer you play them, and the better you do translates into a higher Gamer Level. When you reach certain levels, you can unlock special rewards.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co7ji5.jpg",
        "release_date": 1081123200,
        "rating": 81.91704463180356,
        "rating_count": 8,
        "genres": "Fighting|Sport",
        "platform_ids": "11,8",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/fight-night-2004",
        "cached_at": 1772529809
      },
      {
        "id": 5836,
        "name": "Fight Night Round 3",
        "summary": "EA Sports' Fight Night Round 3 from EA Chicago lets you make your own fighter, train them up, and literally take on the world.\n\nStart by creating your own champ and customizing how they look, what equipment they have, their fighting style, their weight class, their signature move, and even their own illegal hit. Get equipment and trainers for your fighter to enhance his look and performance.\n\nThen take your fighter to career mode where you'll play fight your way up from the local gym all the way up to five-star venues. Get trainers to enhance your training and boost your speed and power. Play against randomly generated fighters all the way up through the ranks till you beat them in points or to a pulp. Certain fights may get you a bit of extra money as an incentive, or give you a promotional deal, but pick your fights carefully because strategy inside the ring won't matter if you mismanage your fisher outside.\n\nFight smart during the fight by using the total punch control system to throw the punches you want to by using the analog stick. The total punch control system maps your fists to the analog stick getting rid of the need for senseless button mashing.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co53v4.jpg",
